"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1726,"**
Narrated to us ‘Īsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ghāfiqī; he said: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb on the authority of Ibn Abī Dhī’b on the authority of Sa‘īd al-Maqburī on the authority of his father on the authority of Abū Hurayrah (RA) that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said:

And it was also narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Rāfi‘; he said: Narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Ismā‘īl ibn Abī Fudayk; he informed us Ibn Abī Dhī’b on the authority of al-Maqburī on the authority of his father on the authority of Abū Hurayrah (RA) that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said:

“No sun has ever risen or set on a day better than Friday. Allāh guided us to it, while other people strayed from it. The people are our followers in it, so it belongs to us. The Jews have Saturday, and the Christians have Sunday. Indeed, in it there is an hour—no believing person prays during it asking Allāh for anything except that He will grant it to him.”

Then he mentioned the hadith."
